    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, we're having an issue with our sublimation heat presses. the ink isn't transferring fully onto the polyester fabric, leaving these patchy, faded spots in the print. we're running at 200c for 40 seconds with about 4 bar of pressure. any idea why the color transfer is failing?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It sounds like the heat setting might be too low for your specific job. Try increasing the heat to 230-245c and extending the duration to 55-85 seconds if your fabric and ink can handle it. This often improves adhesion and color transfer on polyester. Additionally, ensure your ink is properly saturated and the polyester is clean; even small contaminants can affect sublimation prints.",
      "source": "target",
