      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The issue might indeed be with the ink. Sublimation ink typically requires a high level of saturation, so check if the saturation of your ink supplier is consistent and sits properly on the polyester. High absorption rate of polyester could also mean that ink consumption is higher. Make sure to test a sample batch to see if the quality of the ink matches your production needs. If this doesn't resolve the issue, you might want to look into whether your heat press has an uneven heating element, which would affect the color transfer consistency. In that case, having a professional technician inspect your equipment for any possible flaws or considering an equipment upgrade might be necessary.",
